    "answer": "Here are the best phones under ₹40,000 based on the available data:\n\n* **Motorola Edge 70 Pro (₹39,999):** Sitting right at the top of your budget, this phone features a powerful MediaTek Dimensity 8500 Extreme processor, a large 6.80-inch display, and a 50-megapixel front camera. \n* **OPPO Reno 15 (₹35,990):** A top-rated option powered by the MediaTek Dimensity 8450 processor. It comes with a 50-megapixel front camera and a relatively compact 6.32-inch display.\n* **Motorola Edge 70 Fusion (₹30,999):** A slightly more affordable option that offers a large 6.80-inch display, a 50-megapixel + 13-megapixel rear camera setup, and a 32-megapixel front camera.\n\n**Comparison:**\nIf you want the highest performance in this price range, the **Motorola Edge 70 Pro** is the most powerful pick with its Dimensity 8500 Extreme chip and high-resolution front camera. If you prefer a smaller screen size, the **OPPO Reno 15** offers a similar high-resolution 50MP selfie camera in a more compact form factor. For a budget-friendly option that still delivers a large display and versatile cameras, the **Motorola Edge 70 Fusion** is a great value.\n\n*(Note: The Moto G37 Power is also available well under budget at ₹16,999 for entry-level needs, while options like the OnePlus 13s exceed the ₹40,000 limit at ₹51,999).*",
